 "っす": "كَانَ (As a copulative verb:) / كَانَ هُوَ, هِيَ (As a copulative verb:) / كَانَ (As an intransitive lexical verb:)  [be]\nsemi-polite copula",
 "ったら": "إِنْ (supposing that) / لَوْ (supposing that) / إِذَا (supposing that)  [if]\nalso ～だら\nمثال: やってみたら簡単でした。\n→ I found it easy when I gave it a try. / [when it comes to ... ; as for ...]\nindicates light scorn, annoyance, surprise, etc. about a topic\nمثال: うちの父ったら、夜私を一人で外へ出してくれないの。\n→ My father doesn't let me go out alone at night. / [why don't you ... ; why not ...]\nat sentence end\nمثال: ホワイトさんに聞いてみたら？\n→ Why don't you ask Mr White? / [I tell you! ; I said ...]\nat sentence end; adds emphasis; usu. ったら\nمثال: 静かにしろったら。\n→ Do be quiet!",
 "っちゅう": "مَعْنًى (symbolic value of something) / الْمَعْنَى (symbolic value of something) / مَعْنًى (significance of a thing, as \"the meaning of life\") / مَعْنًى (definition or connotation of a word)  [meaning]\ncontraction of（と／って）言う",
