 "てびき": "إِرْشَاد, هِدَايَة (The act or process of guiding.) / هِدَايَة, إِرْشَاد (Advice or counselling on some topic.)  [guidance] / مُقَدَّمَة (The act or process of introducing.) / تَعْرِيف (A means, such as a personal letter, of presenting one person to another.) / مُقَدَّمَة, مَدْخَل (An initial section of a book or article, which introduces the subject material.)  [introduction] / مُرْشِد, مُرْشِد سِيَاحِيّ (Someone who guides, especially someone hired to show people around a place or an) / دَلِيل (A document or book that offers information or instruction; guidebook.) / دَلَّ, هَدَى (To serve as a guide for someone or something; to lead or direct in a way; to con)  [guide]",
 "てびきしょ": "دَلِيل, كُتَيِّب (A topically organized book of reference on a certain field of knowledge, regardl)  [handbook]\nمثال: こういう手引書はもっと分かりやすく書くべきだ。\n→ Such manuals should be written in simpler language.",
 "てびろい": "وَاسِع, رَحْب (Having plenty of space; roomy; capacious.)  [spacious] / كَبِير, وَاسِع (Of considerable or relatively great size or extent.)  [large (scale)]",
 "てふうきん": "أَكُورْدِيُون (a small, portable, keyed wind instrument)  [accordion]",
 "てふき": "مِنْشَفَة (A cloth used for wiping, especially one used for drying anything wet, such as a )  [(hand) towel]",
 "てふだ": "[one's hand] / بِطَاقَة عَمَل, بِطَاقَة مُؤَسَّسَة (A small card with a person's name and professional information (such as occupati)  [business card] / [wallet-sized (photo)]",
 "てぶくろ": "قُفَّاز, كَفّ (An item of clothing, covering all or part of the hand and fingers, but usually a)  [glove]\nمثال: この手袋は両方がそろっていない。\n→ Their gloves are not in pairs.",
 "てぶり": "لَفْتَة, إِشَارَة (A motion of the limbs or body, especially one made to emphasize speech.)  [(hand) gesture]\nمثال: わずか３６ヶ月後に、ココは１８４語にあたる手振りを使うことができた。\n→ After only 36 months, Koko could use 184 signs.",
 "てへん": "قِمَّة (The highest or uppermost part of something.)  [top]\nمثال: 私たちは大阪タワーのてっぺんに上がった。\n→ We got to the top of Osaka Tower. / فَرْوَة اَلرَّأْس (part of head where the hair grows)  [(top of) scalp]\nesp. 頂辺 when in kanji",
 "てほどき": "مُقَدَّمَة (The act or process of introducing.) / تَعْرِيف (A means, such as a personal letter, of presenting one person to another.) / مُقَدَّمَة, مَدْخَل (An initial section of a book or article, which introduces the subject material.)  [introduction]",
 "てほん": "نَمُوذَج (A representation of a physical object.) / نَمُوذَج مُصَغَّر (A simulation used to analyze the workings of a real world system or event.) / نَمُوذَج (A style, type, or design.) / نَمُوذَج (The structural design of a complex system.) / قَدْوَة (A successful example to be copied, with or without modifications.)  [model]\nمثال: 彼の行儀をお手本にしなさい。\n→ Model your manners on his. / [model handwriting ; model drawing]",
 "てま": "وَقْت (A duration of time.) / مَرَّة, مرة (An instant of time.) / وَقْت (An instant of time.) / حِين, وَقْت (A ratio of comparison (see also usage notes and prepositional sense at 'times').)  [time]\nمثال: 食べるのにどうしてそんなに手間がかかるのか。\n→ Why do you take so long to eat? / دَفْع (The act of paying.)  [payment (for labour)] / [tedious job ; troublesome job]",
 "てまえ": "[before oneself ; in front of one]\nمثال: 手前のガラス張りの建物は薔薇園なんです。温室になっていて、いつも薔薇を観賞できるようになってるんですよ。\n→ The glass fronted building before you is the rose garden. It's a greenhouse so you will always be able to appreciate the roses. / [a bit before reaching (a location) ; this side (of a location)]\nمثال: あの信号の手前で降ろしてください。\n→ Please let me off on this side of that traffic light. / وَجْه, مُحَيًّا (The front part of the head of a human or other animal, featuring the eyes, nose,) / مَظْهَر (Public image; outward appearance.) / وَاجَهَ (To deal with (a difficult situation or person); to accept (facts, reality, etc.))  [face]\nمثال: 自分の直感が、いかに確かなものか自慢した手前、当てがはずれた時は首をやらなければならなくなった。\n→ Having boasted how sure his hunches were, he was forced to eat his hat when he guessed wrong. / مَهَارَة (A capacity to do something well; a technique, an ability, usually acquired or le)  [skill]",
 "てまえがって": "أَنَانِيّ (Having excessive or exclusive regard and concern for one's own well-being, profi)  [selfish]",
 "てまえども": "نحن (The sovereign alone in his or her capacity as monarch. (This is the royal we. Th)  [we (esp. used by merchants, etc.)]",
