 "てりかえし": "اِنْعِكَاس, عَكْس (The act of reflecting or the state of being reflected.)  [reflection]",
 "てりかえす": "عَكَسَ (To mirror, or show the image of something.)  [to reflect]\nمثال: 太陽の照り返しが強い。\n→ There's a lot of glare.",
 "てりはえる": "لَمَعَ, وَمَضَ (To emit or reflect light so as to glow.)  [to shine]",
 "てりやき": "تِيرْيَاكِي (A cooking technique used in Japanese cuisine in which foods are broiled or grill)  [teriyaki (meat or fish marinated in sweet soy sauce and broiled)]",
 "てりゅうだん": "قُنْبُلَة, قُنْبُلَة يَدَوِيَّة (A small explosive device, designed to be thrown by hand or launched using a rifl)  [grenade]\nمثال: テロリストが手榴弾を投げる前に爆発してしまい、片腕を吹き飛ばされてしまった。\n→ The grenade blew up before the terrorist could throw it, and his arm was blown off!",
 "てる": "لَمَعَ, وَمَضَ (To emit or reflect light so as to glow.)  [to shine]\nمثال: 降っても照っても明日は出発します。\n→ Rain or shine, I will start tomorrow. / [to look slightly upward (of a noh mask; indicating joy, etc.)]\nfrom 面照る",
 "てれ": "خَجَل, حَيَاء (The quality or property of being bashful)  [bashfulness]",
 "てれくさい": "أَخْجَلَ (To disrupt someone's composure or comfort with acting publicly or freely.)  [embarrassing]\nمثال: 彼は彼女のいる前ではとても照れくさそうにする。\n→ He acts very shy in her presence.",
 "てれしょう": "خَجُول (Shy; not liking to be noticed; socially timid.)  [bashful]",
 "てわたす": "يَد, إيد (That which resembles, or to some extent performs the office of, a human hand.) / عَقْرَب (That which resembles, or to some extent performs the office of, a human hand.) / عَامِل (An agent; a servant, or manual laborer; a workman, trained or competent for spec)  [to hand (over)]\nمثال: 彼女は私に１枚の紙を手渡した。\n→ She handed me a sheet of paper.",
 "てをあげる": "[to raise one's hand]\nمثال: 生徒はあまり手を挙げません。\n→ Students don't raise their hands much. / اِسْتَسْلَمَ (To give oneself up into the power of another, especially as a prisoner; to submi) / اِسْتَسْلَام (An act of surrendering, submission into the possession of another; a feeling of )  [to surrender]\nusu. 手を上げる / [to raise one's hand to someone (as a threat to strike)]\nusu. 手を上げる / حَسَّنَ (To make (something) better; to increase the value or productivity (of something)) / تَحَسَّنَ (To become better.)  [to improve]\nusu. 手を上げる",
 "てをいれる": "صَحِيح, صَوَاب (Free from error; true; accurate.) / صَحَّحَ (To make something that was wrong become right; to remove error from.)  [to correct] / [to put one's hand in (e.g. pocket)]",
 "てをかける": "لَمَسَ (Primarily physical senses.) / لَمْسَة, مُلَامَسَة (An act of touching, especially with the hand or finger.) / لَمْس (The faculty or sense of perception by physical contact.)  [to touch] / اِهْتَمَّ, اِعْتَنَى (To care for; to keep safe.)  [to look after] / سَرَقَ (To take illegally, or without the owner's permission, something owned by someone) / اِسْتَرَقَ (To move silently or secretly; to pass unnoticed.)  [to steal]",
 "てをかす": "مد يد العون (To help or assist, especially voluntarily.)  [to lend a hand]\nمثال: この事件に手を貸してください。\n→ Give me a hand with this case.",
 "てをくむ": "[to join hands together]\nمثال: あなたは膝に手を組んで静かに座っていさえすればよい。\n→ You have only to sit quietly with your hands folded in your lap. / تَعَاوَنَ (To work together with others to achieve a common goal.) / تَعاوَنُ مَعَ العَدُوّ (To voluntarily cooperate treasonably, as with an enemy occupation force in one's)  [to collaborate]",
 "てをくわえる": "[to perform some process ; to apply some treatment] / صَحِيح, صَوَاب (Free from error; true; accurate.) / صَحَّحَ (To make something that was wrong become right; to remove error from.)  [to correct]",
 "てをさしのべる": "مد يد العون (To help or assist, especially voluntarily.)  [to lend a hand]\nمثال: そのわかい男が手を差し伸べたのでわたしはそれを握った。\n→ The young man put out his hand and I shook it.",
 "てをそめる": "بَدَأَ, اِبْتَدَأَ (To start, to initiate or take the first step into something.)  [to begin (with)]\nمثال: そのプロジェクトの責任者であったジェイソンが、汚職に手を染めた理由で解任された。\n→ Jason, who was in charge of the project, was dismissed for corruption.",
 "てをたずさえて": "مَعًا, سَوِيًّا (At the same time, in the same place; in close association or proximity.)  [(acting) together]",
 "てをたたく": "تَصْفِيق (The act of striking the palms of the hands, or any two surfaces, together.) / صَفَّق (To strike the palms of the hands together, creating a sharp sound.) / صَفَّقَ (To applaud.)  [to clap]\nمثال: その生徒たちは皆手をたたいた。\n→ All the students clapped their hands.",
 "てをだす": "[to reach out one's hand ; to extend one's arm]\nمثال: 窓から手を出さないで。\n→ Don't stick your hand out of the window. / [to get involved in ; to embark on]\nمثال: あらゆる職業に手を出す者は何の熟練工にもなれない。\n→ Jack of all trades is master of none. / [to start a fight ; to get physical with]\nمثال: だが、組み手で手を出さないのは優しさではない！！\n→ However not attacking your partner in sparring is not a kindness! / أَخَذَ (To get into one's hands, possession, or control, with or without force.) / أَخَذَ بِـ (To receive or accept (something, especially something which was given).) / اِتَّخَذَ (To receive or accept (something, especially something which was given).) / أَخَذَ (To receive or accept (something, especially something which was given).) / أَخَذَ (To grasp or grip.) / اِسْتَغْرَقَ (To fill or require: to last or expend (an amount of time).)  [to take]\nمثال: 私の金に意地汚く手を出すな。\n→ Don't put your greedy hands on my money.",
 "てをつける": "[to set one's hand to ; to start work on]\nمثال: いずれは手をつけなければならないだろう。\n→ I suppose I've got to get my feet wet sometime. / غَلَّ, اِخْتَلَسَ (To steal or misappropriate money that one has been trusted with, especially to s)  [to embezzle]\nمثال: 州知事は黒い金に手をつけました。\n→ The governor took the money out of a slush fund. / [to have sexual relations ; to have an affair]",
 "てをとおす": "لَبِسَ, اِرْتَدَى (To don (clothing, equipment, or the like).)  [to put on (clothing, esp. new)]\nمثال: まだその上着には手を通してないんだ。\n→ I haven't put on the jacket yet.",
 "てをとりあう": "[to hold hands ; to join hands] / [to do together ; to go arm in arm] / تَعَاوَنَ (To work or act together, especially for a common purpose or benefit.)  [to cooperate]",
 "てをのばす": "بَلَغَ (To extend, stretch, or thrust out (for example a limb or object held in the hand)  [to reach (for)] / [to try one's hand at (something new)]",
 "てをのべる": "مد يد العون (To help or assist, especially voluntarily.)  [to lend a hand]",
 "てをやかせる": "أزْعَجَ (To annoy, to disturb, to irritate; to be troublesome to, to make trouble for.) / يَزْعَجْ, يُضَايِقْ (A mild expression of annoyance.)  [to bother]",
 "てをやすめる": "رَاحَة, اِسْتِرَاحَة (Relief from work or activity by sleeping; sleep.) / اِسْتَرَاحَ (To be based on; to rely on something for proof or explanation) / بَاقِيَّة (remainder) / أَثَارَة (remainder)  [to rest (from work, studying, etc.)]",
 "てをやる": "لَمَسَ (Primarily physical senses.) / لَمْسَة, مُلَامَسَة (An act of touching, especially with the hand or finger.) / لَمْس (The faculty or sense of perception by physical contact.)  [to touch]",
 "てん": "مَرَاسِم, طُقُوس (A ritual, with religious or cultural significance.) / حَفْل رَسْمِيّ (A formal socially established behaviour, often in relation to people of differen)  [ceremony] / [law code] / السُّوَيْد (A country in Scandinavia in Northern Europe. Official name: Kingdom of Sweden. C)  [Sweden]",
 "てんい": "بروفيدنس (capital city of Rhode Island, United States of America)  [providence]",
 "てんいせい": "إِزَاحَة, نُزُوح (The act of displacing, or the state of being displaced; a putting out of place.) / إِزَاحَة (A vector quantity which denotes distance with a directional component.)  [displacement]",
