 "ですが": "لٰكِن, لٰكِنَّ (However, although, nevertheless, on the other hand (introducing a clause contrar) / لٰكِن, وَلٰكِنْ (On the contrary, rather (as a regular adversative conjunction, introducing a wor) / إِلَّا, سِوًى (Except that (introducing a subordinate clause which qualifies a negative stateme) / إلَّا, غَيْرَ (Only; solely; merely.)  [but]\nمثال: 残念ですが、あなたの名前をどうしても覚えられない。\n→ I'm sorry to say I don't remember your name.",
 "ですけど": "لٰكِن, لٰكِنَّ (However, although, nevertheless, on the other hand (introducing a clause contrar) / لٰكِن, وَلٰكِنْ (On the contrary, rather (as a regular adversative conjunction, introducing a wor) / إِلَّا, سِوًى (Except that (introducing a subordinate clause which qualifies a negative stateme) / إلَّا, غَيْرَ (Only; solely; merely.)  [but]\nمثال: 型はいいですけど、色違いはありますか。\n→ The style is nice, but do you have it in a different color?",
