 "とおどおしい": "بَعِيد  [distant (behavior, etc.)]",
 "とおぼえ": "عُوَاء (The act of producing howls.)  [(distant) howling]\nمثال: 昨夜犬の遠吠えが聞こえた。\n→ Last night, I heard dogs howling. / غِيبَة (The action of slandering a person without that person's knowledge.)  [backbiting]\nمثال: 彼の批判は犬の遠吠えだ。\n→ He can only criticize people behind their backs.",
 "とおまわし": "دَوَّار (A road junction at which traffic streams circularly around a central island.)  [roundabout (e.g. expression)]\nمثال: 遠まわしに彼の意見を探った。\n→ I sounded him out about his views.",
 "とおみ": "مَرْقَب, بُرْج الْمُرَاقَبَة (An observation tower in which a lookout keeps watch over prisoners, or looks out)  [watchtower]\nمثال: 山は遠見の方がよい。\n→ Mountains look better viewed from a distance.",
 "とおめ": "[distant view ; looking from a distance] / [being able to see a long distance ; good long-distance vision] / مَدَّ النَّظَرِ (The condition of being unable to focus on near objects; presbyopia.)  [farsightedness]",
 "とおめがね": "[spectacles for far-sightedness] / تِلِسْكُوب, مِقْرَاب (A monocular optical instrument that magnifies distant objects, especially in ast)  [telescope]",
 "とおもうと": "مَا أَن, حَالَمَا (At the moment when; immediately (after); instantly; directly.)  [as soon as]\nafter past tense verb / [at the thought of ; when I think about]",
 "とおもったら": "مَا أَن, حَالَمَا (At the moment when; immediately (after); instantly; directly.)  [as soon as]\nafter past tense verb\nمثال: 彼女がその本を読み始めたと思ったらすぐに、誰かがドアをノックした。\n→ She had hardly begun to read the book before someone knocked at the door. / [at the thought of ; when I think about]\nمثال: もしこれが間違っていると思ったら遠慮なく言いなさい。\n→ If you think this is wrong, you must speak out.",
 "とおり": "شَارِع, زَنَقَة (A paved part of road, usually in a village or a town.)  [street]\nمثال: この通りに沿って行けば駅に着きます。\n→ If you follow this street, you will get to the station. / مُرُور (pedestrians or vehicles on roads or on the air)  [traffic]\nمثال: この横町は人の通りが多い。\n→ This cross street is busy with pedestrian traffic. / تَدَفُّق (the movement of a fluid) / تَدَفَّقَ, سَالَ (To move as a fluid from one position to another.)  [flow (of water, air, etc.)]\nمثال: この煙突は通りが悪くなった。\n→ This chimney has begun to draw badly. / بَلَغَ (To extend, stretch, or thrust out (for example a limb or object held in the hand)  [reach (of voice)]",
 "とおりあめ": "شَتْوَة, مَطْرَة (A brief fall of precipitation (spell of rain, or a similar fall of snow, sleet, ) / مِرَشَّة, دُش (A device for bathing by which water is made to fall on the body from a height, e) / اِسْتَحَمَّ, تَحَمَّمَ (To bathe using a shower.)  [shower]\nمثال: 通り雨だからすぐ止むよ。\n→ This is a tropical storm. It'll be over soon.",
 "とおりあわせる": "صَادَفَ (To find, usually by accident.)  [to come across]",
 "とおりいっぺん": "مَرَّرَ, مَرَّ (To change place.) / اِحْتَازَ (To change in state or status) / اِنْقَضَى, مَرَّ (To move through time.) / أَهمَلَ (To move through time.) / تَغَاضَى (To be accepted.) / تَخَلَّى (To refrain from doing something.) / طَريق (An opening, road, or track, available for passing; especially, one through or ov) / جَوَاز (Permission or license to pass, or to go and come.) / جَوَاز (A document granting permission to pass or to go and come; a passport; a ticket p)  [passing] / فُرْصَة (An opportunity or possibility.)  [chance (e.g. customer)]",
 "とおりがかり": "مَرَّرَ, مَرَّ (To change place.) / اِحْتَازَ (To change in state or status) / اِنْقَضَى, مَرَّ (To move through time.) / أَهمَلَ (To move through time.) / تَغَاضَى (To be accepted.) / تَخَلَّى (To refrain from doing something.) / طَريق (An opening, road, or track, available for passing; especially, one through or ov) / جَوَاز (Permission or license to pass, or to go and come.) / جَوَاز (A document granting permission to pass or to go and come; a passport; a ticket p)  [passing (along the way)]\nمثال: 通りがかりの車が私たちに水をはねた。\n→ A passing car splashed water on us.",
 "とおりがけ": "مَرَّرَ, مَرَّ (To change place.) / اِحْتَازَ (To change in state or status) / اِنْقَضَى, مَرَّ (To move through time.) / أَهمَلَ (To move through time.) / تَغَاضَى (To be accepted.) / تَخَلَّى (To refrain from doing something.) / طَريق (An opening, road, or track, available for passing; especially, one through or ov) / جَوَاز (Permission or license to pass, or to go and come.) / جَوَاز (A document granting permission to pass or to go and come; a passport; a ticket p)  [passing (along the way)]\nمثال: 通りがけに本屋によった。\n→ I entered the bookstore on the way.",
 "とおりすぎる": "مَرَّرَ, مَرَّ (To change place.) / اِحْتَازَ (To change in state or status) / اِنْقَضَى, مَرَّ (To move through time.) / أَهمَلَ (To move through time.) / تَغَاضَى (To be accepted.) / تَخَلَّى (To refrain from doing something.) / طَريق (An opening, road, or track, available for passing; especially, one through or ov) / جَوَاز (Permission or license to pass, or to go and come.) / جَوَاز (A document granting permission to pass or to go and come; a passport; a ticket p)  [to pass]\nمثال: 私はその暗い道を通り過ぎた。\n→ I passed over the dark street.",
 "とおりぬける": "اِخْتَرَقَ, نَفَذَ (To go through, to travel through, to transit or lie across a place or from one p)  [to pass through]\nمثال: その車は門を通り抜けた。\n→ The car passed through a gate.",
 "とおりまてき": "عَشْوَائِيّ (Occurring for no particular reason; haphazard, unpredictable.) / عَشْوَائِيّ (Involving an outcome which is impossible to predict, but which may be represente)  [random (e.g. attack, killing)]",
 "とおりみち": "قِطْعَة (A paragraph or section of text or music with particular meaning.)  [passage]\nمثال: 警官が通り道を空けて車を通した。\n→ Policemen cleared the way to let cars pass.",
 "とおり道": "قِطْعَة (A paragraph or section of text or music with particular meaning.)  [passage]\nمثال: 警官が通り道を空けて車を通した。\n→ Policemen cleared the way to let cars pass.",
 "とおる": "[to go by ; to go past]\nمثال: 私は毎日その教会の前を通る。\n→ I go by that church every day. / رَكَضَ (to move quickly on two feet) / جَرَى (to move quickly on two feet)  [to run (between; of a rail service, bus route, etc.)]\nمثال: 駅と飛行機の間は、バスが通っている。\n→ Buses run between the station and the airport. / [to go indoors ; to go into a room] / اِخْتَرَقَ (To enter into; to make way into the interior of; to pierce.)  [to penetrate]\nمثال: 弾がヘルメットを通った。\n→ A bullet pierced the helmet.",
 "とか": "هَكَذَا (Like, of the kind mentioned.)  [such as]\noft. as ...とか...とか\nمثال: 包丁とか鍋とか、台所用品を持参すること。\n→ Don't forget to bring kitchen utensils such as knives and cooking pots. / ا (The first numeral symbol of the English alphabet, called ay and written in the L) / إِي, آ (The name of the Latin script letter A/a.) / فِي (To do with time; Each, per, in, on, by. Often occurs between two nouns, where th)  [a (certain)]\nused to convey hearsay or uncertain information; oft. with 言う, 聞く, etc.\nمثال: マルコーニさんとかいう人がご面会です。\n→ A Mr. Marconi wants to see you. / [I hear that ... ; people say that ...]\nat sentence end / [or something ; something like]\nused to make a statement vague or less absolute; usu. after a noun",
 "とかい": "مَدِينَة, بَلَد (A large settlement, bigger than a town; sometimes with a specific legal definiti)  [city]\nمثال: あの人達は都会の生活にあこがれている。\n→ They are longing for city life. / [Tokyo Metropolitan Assembly]",
 "とかいか": "تَمَدُّن, تَحَضُّر (The process of the formation and growth of cities.)  [urbanization]",
 "とかいてき": "حَضَرِيّ, مَدَنِيّ (Of, pertaining to, characteristic of, or happening or located in, a city or town)  [urban]\nمثال: 住民達は彼らの都会的な文化に誇りを持っている。\n→ The inhabitants are proud of their urban culture.",
 "とかいは": "حَضَرِيّ, مَدَنِيّ (Of, pertaining to, characteristic of, or happening or located in, a city or town)  [urban]\nمثال: 彼女は中年の都会派プロフェッショナルでした。\n→ She was a middle-aged urban professional.",
 "とかく": "[(doing) various things ; (doing) this and that]\nمثال: あの人にはとかくのうわさがあった。\n→ There were some unsavory rumors about him. / [being apt to ; being prone to]\nمثال: 運動が健康の鍵であるのを私たちはとかく忘れがちだ。\n→ We tend to forget that exercise is a key to good health. / عَلَى كُلِّ حَال, على كل حال (Regardless; anyhow.) / عَلَى أَيُّ حَالٍ, على كل حال (Used to indicate that a statement explains or supports a previous statement. See)  [anyway] / مُخْتَلِف, مُتَنَوَّع (Having a broad range (of different elements).)  [various]",
 "とかげざ": "سِحْلِيَّة, ضَبّ (Any reptile of the order Squamata that is not a snake or mosasaur—typically char)  [the Lizard]",
