 "とかす": "ذَابَ, انْصَهَرَ (To change (or to be changed) from a solid state to a liquid state, usually by a )  [to melt]\nمثال: ４．中華鍋にごま油を熱してバターを溶かす。\n→ 4. Heat the sesame oil in the wok and melt the butter. / [to dissolve (in a liquid) ; to bring into solution]\nمثال: 彼はコーヒーに砂糖を溶かした。\n→ He dissolved some sugar in his coffee. / فَقَدَ (To cease to have (something) in one's possession or capability.) / خَسِرَ (To become a defeated competitor in (a game, competition, trial, etc).) / خَسِرَ (To be defeated (in a game, competition, contest, etc.))  [to lose (money; through gambling, etc.)]",
 "とかなんとか": "أَوْ كَمَا قَالَ (used to indicate a paraphrase or the chance of an error in the details of report)  [or words to that effect] / [something or other]",
