 "ときすすめる": "أَقْنَعَ (To successfully convince (someone) to agree to, accept, or do something, usually)  [to persuade]\nمثال: 教師は生徒に善行をするように説き勧めた。\n→ The teacher exhorted his pupils to do well.",
 "ときたま": "أَحْيَانًا (On occasion: at relatively infrequent intervals, from time to time, sometimes.)  [occasionally]\nمثال: ときたま彼から便りがあります。\n→ I hear from him once in a while.",
 "ときつける": "أَقْنَعَ (To successfully convince (someone) to agree to, accept, or do something, usually)  [to persuade]\nمثال: 彼に家業を継ぐようにときつけた。\n→ I persuaded him to take on the family business.",
 "ときとして": "أَحْيَانًا, سَاعَات (On some occasions, over some periods, or in certain circumstances, but not alway)  [sometimes]\nمثال: 天才は時として態度が粗野なことがある。\n→ A genius can sometimes have rude manners.",
 "ときどき": "أَحْيَانًا, سَاعَات (On some occasions, over some periods, or in certain circumstances, but not alway)  [sometimes]\nمثال: ジェーンはときどき学校まで走っていく。\n→ Jane sometimes runs to school. / مُنَاسِب (Suitable or fit; proper; felicitous.) / لَائِق (Suitable to the social situation or to social respect or social discreetness; so)  [appropriate (for the season or occasion)]",
 "ときならぬ": "مُفَاجِئ (Not expected, anticipated or foreseen.)  [unexpected]\nمثال: 「冬のソナタ」を例に挙げるまでもなく、いまや時ならぬ韓流ブームである。\n→ You don't need to bring up \"A Winter Sonata\" to show that South Korean culture is having an unexpected boom in Japan.",
 "ときに": "بِالْمُنَاسَبَةِ, عَلَى فِكْرَةٍ (Incidentally; used in referencing a parenthetical statement not timely, central,)  [by the way]\nمثال: 時に鈴木の件について聞いたか。\n→ By the way, have you heard about Suzuki? / أَحْيَانًا, سَاعَات (On some occasions, over some periods, or in certain circumstances, but not alway)  [sometimes]\nمثال: 犯罪は時に法律を知らないために引き起こされる。\n→ Crimes sometimes result from ignorance of the law. / بِدِقَّة (In a precise manner; exactly.)  [precisely (at that time)]",
 "ときには": "أَحْيَانًا (On occasion, sometimes.)  [at times]\nمثال: ときには試合は一日中続きました。\n→ Sometimes the game lasted all day.",
