 "となる": "صَارَ, أَصْبَحَ (begin to be; turn into (often with permanent states).)  [to become]\nمثال: すべては燃えて灰となった。\n→ Everything was burnt to ashes.",
 "とに": "مُبَاغِت, مُفَاجِئ (Occurring quickly with little or no warning or expectation; instantly.)  [sudden]",
 "とにかく": "عَلَى كُلِّ حَال, على كل حال (Regardless; anyhow.) / عَلَى أَيُّ حَالٍ, على كل حال (Used to indicate that a statement explains or supports a previous statement. See)  [anyway]\nمثال: とにかく、試験が終わってほっとしたよ。\n→ Anyhow, I'm relieved the test is over. / [setting aside ... ; regardless of ...]\nas ...は〜 or ...なら〜 / حَقًّا (Actually; in fact; in reality.) / وَٱللّٰه؟ (indicating surprise at, or requesting confirmation of, some ) / لَيْسَ مَعْقُل! (indicating surprise at, or requesting confirmation of, some ) / حَقًّا (indicating surprise at, or requesting confirmation of, some )  [really]",
