 "とりあう": "وَصَلَ (To connect or combine into one; to put together.) / اِتَّصَلَ (To come together; to meet.) / اِلْتَحَقَ بِـ, اِنْضَمَّ إِلَى (To become a member of.)  [to join (hands)]\nas 手を〜\nمثال: 私の望みは、世界中の人々がいつの日か手を取り合うことだ。\n→ My wish is that one day all the people in world will go hand in hand. / [to scramble for ; to struggle for] / [to pay attention to ; to take notice of]\nusu. in the negative",
 "とりあえず": "أَوَّلًا, قَبْلَ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ (Firstly; before anything else.)  [first of all]\nمثال: とりあえずこれをやってしまおう。\n→ Let's do this first of all. / [for now ; for the time being] / عَلَى كُلِّ حَال, على كل حال (Regardless; anyhow.) / عَلَى أَيُّ حَالٍ, على كل حال (Used to indicate that a statement explains or supports a previous statement. See)  [anyway]",
 "とりあげ": "تَبَنٍّ (The state of being adopted; the acceptance of a child of other parents as if the)  [adoption] / قَبَالَة (The practice and science of being a midwife.)  [midwifery]",
 "とりあげる": "قَطَفَ (To lift; to grasp and raise.)  [to pick up]\nمثال: 彼女はガラスの花瓶を取り上げた。\n→ She picked up one of the glass vases. / تَبَنَّى (To take or receive as one's own what is not so naturally.)  [to adopt (a proposal)]\nsometimes written as 採り上げる\nمثال: 明日の会議では、新しい営業戦略を採り上げる予定です。\n→ In tomorrow's meeting, we're planning to adopt a new marketing strategy. / [to take issue with ; to make a problem of] / وَصَفَ, أَبْلَغَ (To relate details of (an event or incident); to recount, describe (something).) / أَبْلَغَ (To notify someone of (particular intelligence, suspicions, illegality, misconduc) / تَقْرِير, بَلَاغ (A piece of information describing, or an account of certain events given or pres)  [to report (news)]\nمثال: 全新聞がその事件を大きく取り上げた。\n→ All the papers featured the case.",
 "とりあつかい": "مُعَامَلَة (The process or manner of treating someone or something.) / عِلَاج, مُعَالَجَة (Medical care for an illness or injury.)  [treatment]\nمثال: 先生は彼女に正当な取り扱いをしなかった。\n→ The teacher didn't do her justice.",
 "とりあつかいしょ": "فَاعِلِيَّة (The capacity, condition, or state of acting or of exerting power.) / وِكَالَة (The office or function of an agent; also, the relationship between a principal a) / وَكَالَة (An establishment engaged in doing business for another; also, the place of busin) / دَائِرَة (A department or other administrative unit of a government; also, the office or h)  [agency]",
 "とりあつかいじょ": "فَاعِلِيَّة (The capacity, condition, or state of acting or of exerting power.) / وِكَالَة (The office or function of an agent; also, the relationship between a principal a) / وَكَالَة (An establishment engaged in doing business for another; also, the place of busin) / دَائِرَة (A department or other administrative unit of a government; also, the office or h)  [agency]",
 "とりあつかいてん": "قَاسِم (One who or that which distributes.)  [distributor] / فَاعِلِيَّة (The capacity, condition, or state of acting or of exerting power.) / وِكَالَة (The office or function of an agent; also, the relationship between a principal a) / وَكَالَة (An establishment engaged in doing business for another; also, the place of busin) / دَائِرَة (A department or other administrative unit of a government; also, the office or h)  [agency]",
 "とりあつかいてんぽ": "قَاسِم (One who or that which distributes.)  [distributor] / فَاعِلِيَّة (The capacity, condition, or state of acting or of exerting power.) / وِكَالَة (The office or function of an agent; also, the relationship between a principal a) / وَكَالَة (An establishment engaged in doing business for another; also, the place of busin) / دَائِرَة (A department or other administrative unit of a government; also, the office or h)  [agency]",
 "とりあつかいにん": "فَاعِل (One who exerts power, or has the power to act.)  [agent]",
 "とりあつかう": "مِقْبَض (The part of an object which is (designed to be) held in the hand when used or mo)  [to handle]\nمثال: 算数は数を取り扱う。\n→ Arithmetic deals with numbers. / أَدَارَ (To direct or be in charge of.)  [to manage] / عَالَجَ (To care for medicinally or surgically; to apply medical care to.)  [to treat (someone)] / حَمَلَ (To lift (something) and take it to another place; to transport (something) by li)  [to carry]",
 "とりあつめ": "مَجْمُوعَة, جَمْع (A set of items or amount of material procured, gathered or presented together.) / جَمْع (The activity of collecting.)  [collection]",
 "とりあつめる": "جَمَعَ (To bring parts of a whole closer.)  [to gather]\nمثال: 卵を取り集めるのが彼の仕事だ。\n→ It was his job to gather eggs.",
 "とりいそぐ": "عَجَلَة (A rushed action.) / أَسْرَعَ, اِنْدَفَعَ (To do things quickly.)  [to hurry]",
 "とりいる": "تَمَلَّقَ (To flatter, especially with the intent of personal gain.)  [to butter up]\nمثال: 私は彼女に取り入ってうまく秘密を聞き出した。\n→ I charmed a secret out of her.",
 "とりいれ": "حِصَاد (The process of gathering the ripened crop; harvesting.) / مَحْصُول, غَلَّة (The yield of harvesting, i.e., the gathered crops or fruits.) / حَصَدَ (To bring in a harvest; reap; glean.)  [harvesting]\nمثال: 取り入れ時には天気がよかった。\n→ The weather was good for the harvest.",
 "とりいれる": "[to take in ; to gather in]\nمثال: 洗濯物を中へ取り入れて下さい。\n→ Please bring in the washing. / تَبَنَّى (To take or receive as one's own what is not so naturally.)  [to adopt (e.g. an idea)]\nalso written as 採り入れる\nمثال: 私達はいつも彼の忠告を取り入れるというわけではない。\n→ We do not always take his advice. / حِصَاد (The process of gathering the ripened crop; harvesting.) / مَحْصُول, غَلَّة (The yield of harvesting, i.e., the gathered crops or fruits.) / حَصَدَ (To bring in a harvest; reap; glean.)  [to harvest]\nocc. written as 穫り入れる",
 "とりうちぼう": "قُبَّعَة, قُبَّعة (A large size of writing paper.)  [(hunting) cap]",
 "とりえ": "مَاثَلَ (Having a value of; proper to be exchanged for.) / اِسْتَحَقَّ, اِسْتَأْهَلَ (Deserving of.) / اِسْتَحَقَّ (Making a fair equivalent of, repaying or compensating.) / قِيمَة (Value.)  [worth]\nمثال: 天真爛漫なところが彼の唯一の取り柄だな。\n→ Naivete is his only merit.",
 "とりおき": "اِحْتِيَاط (that which is reserved or kept back, as for future use) / ذَخِيرَة (that which is reserved or kept back, as for future use) / حَجَزَ (To book in advance; to make a reservation for.)  [reserving]",
 "とりおく": "[to set aside ; to keep in reserve] / مُرَبًّى (A sweet spread made of any of a variety of fruits.) / حَافَظَ (To protect; to keep from harm or injury.)  [to preserve] / [to put in ; to lay in] / مَسَكَ, مسك (To grasp or grip.)  [to hold]",
 "とりおこなう": "مَسَكَ, مسك (To grasp or grip.)  [to hold (a ceremony)]\nمثال: 教会では儀式が執り行われた。\n→ Rituals were performed in churches.",
 "とりおさえる": "إِسْتَوْلَى عَلَى (To deliberately take hold of; to grab or capture.)  [to seize]\nمثال: 警官はその泥棒を取り押さえた。\n→ The policeman caught the thief. / طَوَّعَ, تَغَلَّبَ عَلَى (To overcome, quieten, or bring under control.)  [to subdue]",
 "とりおとす": "قَطْرَة (small quantity of liquid, just large enough to hold its own ) / نُقْطَة (small quantity of liquid, just large enough to hold its own ) / أَسْقَطَ (to let (something) fall; to allow (something) to fall (eithe)  [to drop]",
 "とりおどし": "فَزَّاعَة (An effigy, typically made of straw and dressed in old clothes, fixed to a pole i)  [scarecrow]",
 "とりおろす": "أَدْنَى, دُنْيَا (Bottom; more towards the bottom than the middle of an object.) / أَنْزَلَ (To let descend by its own weight, as something suspended; to let down.)  [to lower]",
 "とりかい": "تَرْبِيَة الطُيُور (The rearing and care of birds (especially poultry))  [aviculture]",
 "とりかえ": "مُبَادَلَة (To exchange or give (something) in an non-normal exchange (for something else).)  [swap]",
 "とりかえし": "شِفَاء, تَعَافِي (A return to normal health.)  [recovery]",
 "とりかえす": "شُفِيَ, بَرِئَ (To get better, to regain health or prosperity.)  [to recover]\nمثال: 私は彼からお金を取り返した。\n→ I got the money back from him.",
 "とりかえっこ": "مُبَادَلَة (To exchange or give (something) in an non-normal exchange (for something else).)  [swap]\nمثال: 君のラジオを僕の自転車と取り替えっこしないか。\n→ Will you give me your radio for my bicycle?",
 "とりかえる": "تَبْدِيل, تَبَادُل (An act of exchanging or trading.) / بُورْصَة, تَدَاوُل (A place for conducting trading.) / تَبَادَلَ, صَرَفَ (To trade or barter.)  [to exchange]\nمثال: これを青いのと取り替えてください。\n→ Please change this for a blue one. / اِسْتَبْدَلَ, بَدَّلَ (To supply or substitute an equivalent with.)  [to replace]\nمثال: 彼らは欠陥テレビを新しいのと取りかえた。\n→ They replaced the defective TV with a new one.",
 "とりかかる": "بَدَأَ, اِبْتَدَأَ (To start, to initiate or take the first step into something.)  [to begin (doing)]\nمثال: 彼は犬小屋作りに取りかかった。\n→ He went about making a doghouse.",
 "とりかこむ": "أَحَاطَ, حَفَّ (To encircle something or simultaneously extend in all directions.)  [to surround]\nمثال: 彼は群衆に取り囲まれた。\n→ He was surrounded by the crowd.",
 "とりかじ": "مِينَاء, مينا (A place on the coast at which ships can shelter, or dock to load and unload carg) / مَنْفَذ (A logical or physical construct in and from which data are transferred. Computer) / كَيَّفَ, غَيَّرَ (To adapt, modify, or recode to work on a different platform.)  [port (side of a ship)]",
 "とりかぶと": "بِيش (The herb wolfsbane, or monkshood; any plant of the genus Aconitum, all the speci)  [aconite (esp. species Aconitum japonicum)] / [traditional bugaku hat]",
 "とりかわす": "تَبْدِيل, تَبَادُل (An act of exchanging or trading.) / بُورْصَة, تَدَاوُل (A place for conducting trading.) / تَبَادَلَ, صَرَفَ (To trade or barter.)  [to exchange]",
 "とりき": "طَبَقَة (single thickness of some material covering a surface)  [layering (a plant)]",
 "とりきめ": "قَرَار, تَصْمِيم (A choice or judgement.)  [decision]\nمثال: １５年間は満足しうる取り決めであった。\n→ It was a satisfactory arrangement for fifteen years.",
 "とりきめる": "وَافَقَ (To be in harmony about an opinion, statement, or action; to have a consistent id)  [to agree]\nمثال: その２国は平和条約を取り決めた。\n→ The two countries negotiated a peace treaty.",
 "とりきる": "[to take completely ; to deplete] / عَزَلَ (To set apart or cut off from others.)  [to isolate]",
 "とりく": "ذَبْح (The killing of animals, generally for food.) / ذَبَحَ (To butcher animals, generally for food.)  [slaughter (of animals)]",
 "とりくいぐも": "رُتَيْل (Any of the large, hairy New World spiders comprising the family Theraphosidae.) / رُتَيْل (A species of wolf spider, Lycosa tarantula, native to southern Europe, the mildl)  [tarantula (any spider of family Theraphosidae)] / [bird spider (Avicularia avicularia)]",
 "とりくずす": "هَدَمَ (To destroy (buildings, etc.), especially in a planned or intentional fashion.)  [to demolish] / [to draw on (one's savings, etc.) little by little ; to break into (a reserve fund, etc.)]\nمثال: クリントン陣営は、両州でオバマが取った白人票を取り崩そうと必死になった。\n→ The Clinton camp became desperate to eliminate the white votes Obama had got in both states.",
 "とりくち": "أُسْلُوب, تِقْنِيَة (The practical aspects of a given art, occupation etc.; formal requirements.)  [technique]",
 "とりくみ": "جَهْد, جُهْد (The work involved in performing an activity; exertion.)  [effort]\nمثال: 社長が社員の主体的な取り組みを促した。\n→ The president urged employees to act on their initiative. / مُبَارَاة (Any contest or trial of strength or skill, or to determine superiority.) / شَحّاطَة, شَخَّاطَة (Synonym of fuse, a long wick used to transfer flame to an explosive device.)  [match]\noft. 取組 when in ref. to sumo",
 "とりくむ": "[to grapple with ; to wrestle with] / عَالَجَ (To face or deal with, attempting to overcome or fight down.)  [to tackle (e.g. a problem)]\nمثال: そろそろ本気で仕事に取り組むころだよ。\n→ It is time you get down to work.",
 "とりけし": "اِنْسِحَاب (An act of withdrawing or a state of being withdrawn.)  [withdrawal]",
 "とりけす": "أَلْغَى, أَبْطَلَ (To invalidate or annul something.)  [to cancel]\nمثال: ごめん、取り消すよ。\n→ I'm sorry. I take back my words.",
 "とりげ": "رَخْت (The feathers covering the body of a bird collectively.) / رَخْت (A person's dress, especially when elaborate or fine.)  [plumage] / [decorative feathers on a spear sheath or pole]",
 "とりこ": "أَسِير, أَسِيرَة (One who has been captured or is otherwise confined.) / أَسِير, مَحْبُوس (Held prisoner; not free; confined.)  [captive] / ضَحِيَّة (one who is harmed) / أُضْحِيَّة (a living being slain and offered as a sacrifice)  [victim (of love, etc.)]\nمثال: その音楽は全員をとりこにした。\n→ The music lured everyone.",
 "とりこみ": "[taking in ; bringing in] / أَسْر (An act of capturing; a seizing by force or stratagem.) / أَسَرَ (To take control of; to seize by force or stratagem.)  [capturing (e.g. customers)] / اِلْتِبَاس (A lack of clarity or order.) / اِرْتِبَاك (The state of being confused; misunderstanding.)  [confusion] / وَارِدَات (Something brought in from an exterior source, especially for sale or trade.) / اِسْتِيرَاد, تَوْرِيد (The practice of importing.) / اِسْتَوْرَدَ, وَرَّدَ (To bring (something) in from a foreign country, especially for sale or trade.)  [importing (e.g. data)]",
 "とりこみごと": "اِلْتِبَاس (A lack of clarity or order.) / اِرْتِبَاك (The state of being confused; misunderstanding.)  [confusion]",
 "とりこむ": "تَبَنَّى (To take or receive as one's own what is not so naturally.)  [to adopt (e.g. behaviour)]\nمثال: もし雨になったら洗濯物を取り込んでね。\n→ If it rains, take the washing in. / أَسْر (An act of capturing; a seizing by force or stratagem.) / أَسَرَ (To take control of; to seize by force or stratagem.)  [to capture (e.g. image)] / أَرْضَى, أَعْجَبَ (To make happy or satisfy; to give pleasure to.) / مِن فَضْلِك (interjection to make a polite request) / رَجَاءً (interjection to make a polite request) / لَو سَمَحْت (interjection to make a polite request) / لُطْفًا (interjection to make a polite request) / أَرْجُوك (interjection to make a polite request)  [to please] / غَشَّ, جَدَعَ (To defraud.) / غَشَّ, جَدَعَ (To obtain (money or property) by fraudulent or deceitful methods.)  [to swindle]",
 "とりこめる": "أَحَاطَ, حَفَّ (To encircle something or simultaneously extend in all directions.)  [to surround]",
 "とりこわし": "هَدْم (The process of demolishing or destroying buildings or other structures.)  [demolition]\nمثال: もし建物の取り壊しが無制限に行われるなら、美しい町が単なるコンクリート・ジャングルになる危険があるのである。\n→ If the demolition of buildings is uncontrolled, a fine city is in danger of becoming nothing more than a concrete jungle.",
 "とりこわす": "هَدَمَ (To destroy (buildings, etc.), especially in a planned or intentional fashion.)  [to demolish]\nمثال: その古い建物は取り壊された。\n→ The old building was broken down.",
 "とりさげ": "اِنْسِحَاب (An act of withdrawing or a state of being withdrawn.)  [withdrawal]",
 "とりさげる": "سَحَبَ (To extract (money) from a bank account or other financial deposit.) / تَرَاجَعَ (Chiefly followed by from: to leave a place, someone's presence, etc., to go to a)  [to withdraw]\nمثال: 若さゆえに彼に対する告訴は取り下げられた。\n→ The charges against him were dropped because of his youth.",
 "とりさばく": "اِسْتَعْمَرَ (to fix one's dwelling) / اِسْتَوْطَنَ (to fix one's dwelling) / اِسْتَقَرَّ (to fix one's dwelling)  [to settle (a matter)]",
 "とりさる": "نَقَلَ (to take away) / أَزَالَ (to take away) / أَخْرَجَ (to take away) / جَذَبَ (to take away)  [to remove]\nمثال: 彼はジョージから新聞を取り去った。\n→ He took the newspaper away from George.",
 "とりざた": "تَكَلَّمَ, تَحَدَّثَ (To communicate, usually by means of speech.) / مُحَاضَرَة (A lecture.) / خِطَاب (A major topic of social discussion.) / مُحَادَثَات, مُفَاوَضَات (Meeting to discuss a particular matter.)  [talk (of the town)]",
 "とりしきる": "أَدَارَ (To direct or be in charge of.)  [to manage (all by oneself)]\nمثال: ウイリアムズ氏がその課を取り仕切っている。\n→ Mr Williams carries that section.",
 "とりしずめる": "صَامِت, هَادِئ (With little or no sound; free of disturbing noise.)  [to quiet]",
 "とりしまり": "سَيْطَرَ (To exercise influence over; to suggest or dictate the behavior of.) / تَحَكُّم, مُرَاقَبَة (An influence or authority over something.)  [control]\nمثال: 警察は違法駐車の取り締まりを始めた。\n→ The police began a crackdown on illegal parking.",
 "とりしまりやくかい": "مَجْلِس إِدَارَة (A group of people elected by stockholders to establish corporate policies and ma)  [board of directors]\nمثال: 取締役会は業務執行に関する意思決定を目的としたものだ。\n→ The Board of Directors aim is to make decisions regarding business affairs of the company. / [board of directors' meeting]",
 "とりしまる": "أَدَارَ (To direct or be in charge of.)  [to manage]\nمثال: 市は飲酒運転を非常に厳しく取り締まって、罰金を課している。\n→ The city is cracking down on drunk drivers and giving them fines. / ضَبَطَ (To adjust (a mechanism) for accurate and proper functioning.)  [to regulate]",
 "とりしらべ": "تَحْقِيق (The act of investigating; the process of inquiring into or following up; researc)  [investigation (e.g. by police or prosecutors)]",
 "とりしらべかん": "مُحَقِّق, مُحَقِّقَة (One who investigates.)  [investigator]",
 "とりしらべる": "فَحَصَ, اِمْتَحَنَ (To observe carefully or critically to learn about someone or something.)  [to examine]\nمثال: 事件の原因を取り調べるために実情調査委員会が作られた。\n→ A fact-finding committee was set up to determine the cause of the incident.",
 "とりしろ": "جُزْء (An allocated amount.)  [portion]",
 "とりすてる": "طَرَحَ (To discard (trash, garbage, or the like), to toss out, to put in the trash.)  [to throw away]",
 "とりそこなう": "أَخْطَأَ (To fail to hit, catch, grasp, etc.) / فَاتَ (To fail to experience, attend, partake, take advantage of, etc.) / اِفْتَقَدَ, اِشْتَاقَ (To become aware of the loss or absence of; to feel the want or need of, sometime) / آنِسَة (An unmarried woman; a girl.)  [to miss]\nمثال: 彼女はいつもボールを取り損なってばかりいる。\n→ She is always missing the ball. / أَخْطَأَ (To fail to hit, catch, grasp, etc.) / فَاتَ (To fail to experience, attend, partake, take advantage of, etc.) / اِفْتَقَدَ, اِشْتَاقَ (To become aware of the loss or absence of; to feel the want or need of, sometime) / آنِسَة (An unmarried woman; a girl.)  [to miss (the meaning)]",
 "とりそこねる": "أَخْطَأَ (To fail to hit, catch, grasp, etc.) / فَاتَ (To fail to experience, attend, partake, take advantage of, etc.) / اِفْتَقَدَ, اِشْتَاقَ (To become aware of the loss or absence of; to feel the want or need of, sometime) / آنِسَة (An unmarried woman; a girl.)  [to miss]",
 "とりそろえる": "جَمَعَ (To bring parts of a whole closer.)  [to gather]",
 "とりたて": "مَجْمُوعَة, جَمْع (A set of items or amount of material procured, gathered or presented together.) / جَمْع (The activity of collecting.)  [collection (of a debt, rent, taxes, etc.)] / [selection (for a position) ; exceptional promotion] / طَازَج, طَازَة (Newly produced or obtained; recent.) / عَذْب (Without salt; not saline.)  [fresh]",
 "とりたてて": "خُصُوصًا, خَاصَّةً (Particularly; to a greater extent than is normal.)  [especially]\nusu. with neg. sentence\nمثال: 私は取り立てて騒ぎ立てられるのは好きではない。\n→ I don't like to be made a fuss about.",
 "とりたてる": "جَمَعَ (To gather together; amass.)  [to collect (debts)]\nمثال: 王は人民から税を厳しく取り立てた。\n→ The king exacted taxes from his people. / رَقَّى (To raise (someone) to a more important, responsible, or remunerative job or rank) / رَوَّجَ (To advocate or urge on behalf of (something or someone); to attempt to populariz)  [to promote] / شَدَّدَ (To stress, give emphasis or extra weight to (something).)  [to emphasize]",
 "とりだしボタン": "حِمْل (A burden; a weight to be carried.) / حِمْل (The electrical current or power delivered by a device.) / عَبَّأَ, شَحَنَ (To put a load on or in (a means of conveyance or a place of storage).)  [load]",
 "とりだす": "أَخْرَجَ (To remove.)  [to take out]\nمثال: もう一つの面白いエネルギー源は、放射能の廃棄物質から取り出せる熱である。\n→ Another interesting source of energy is the heat that can be recovered from radioactive waste material. / جَلَبَ (To retrieve; to bear towards; to go and get.)  [to fetch]\nمثال: 適合率とは取り出した記事のうち、どの程度の記事が検索条件に合っているかを示す指標です。\n→ The precision ratio is an index that indicates how many articles meet the search criteria out of all of the articles retrieved.",
 "とりちがえ": "أَسَاء اَلْفَهْم, أَخْطَأَ (To understand wrongly, taking one thing or person for another.) / خَطَأ, غَلْطَة (An error.)  [mistake] / سُوء فَهْم (A mistake as to the meaning of something or a specific point of view; erroneous )  [misunderstanding]",
