 "とりつぎてん": "فَاعِلِيَّة (The capacity, condition, or state of acting or of exerting power.) / وِكَالَة (The office or function of an agent; also, the relationship between a principal a) / وَكَالَة (An establishment engaged in doing business for another; also, the place of busin) / دَائِرَة (A department or other administrative unit of a government; also, the office or h)  [agency]",
 "とりつく": "[to cling to ; to hold on to]\nمثال: メイドは客を一人一人大声でとりついた。\n→ The maid announced each guest. / [to grapple] / بَدَأَ, اِبْتَدَأَ (To start, to initiate or take the first step into something.)  [to begin] / مَلَكَ, اِمْتَلَكَ (To have (something) as, or as if as, an owner; to have, to own.)  [to possess (someone; of an evil spirit, idea, etc.)]\nalso written as 取り憑く",
 "とりつくろう": "[to keep up (appearances) ; to put up (a good front)]\nمثال: 取り繕うように、笑ってみせる。\n→ She smiled to smooth things over. / [to smooth over (a mistake, fault, etc.) ; to gloss over] / أَصْلَحَ (To physically repair (something that is broken, defaced, decayed, torn, or other)  [to mend]",
 "とりつぐ": "أَبْلَغَ, نَقَلَ (To communicate; to make known; to portray.)  [to convey] / بَلَّغَ, أَبْلَغَ (To communicate knowledge to.)  [to inform (of a visitor, phone call, etc.)] / مِقْبَض (The part of an object which is (designed to be) held in the hand when used or mo)  [to handle (goods; for a company)]",
