 "とんがった": "نُقْطَة (A small dot or mark.) / نُقْطَة (A small discrete division or individual feature of something.) / مَوْقِع (A small discrete division or individual feature of something.) / أَشَارَ (To extend the index finger in the direction of something in order to show where )  [pointed]\nمثال: きつつきは、長く尖ったくちばしで、木の幹をつついて、中にいる虫を食べます。\n→ Woodpeckers peck tree trunks with their long pointed beaks and eat insects found there. / حَادّ (Terminating in a point or edge, especially one that can cut or pierce easily; no)  [sharp (voice, words, etc.)] / مُسْتَفِز (Serving or tending to elicit a strong, often negative sentiment in another perso)  [provocative] / نَصْل (The sharp edge of the blade of a knife or other cutting tool.)  [cutting edge]",
 "とんがらし": "نَبَات فُلْفُل (plant of the genus Capsicum (only terms covering capsicum in) / فُلَيْفِلَة (plant of the genus Capsicum (only terms covering capsicum in)  [capsicum (Capsicum annuum, esp. the cultivated chili peppers)]\nمثال: とうがらしで舌がひりひりした。\n→ The chili burnt my tongue. / [shichimi pepper]",
