 "とんちんかん": "سَخَافَة (The quality of being absurd or inconsistent with obvious truth, reason, or sound)  [absurdity]\nمثال: 私の祖父は耳が遠いので、よくトンチンカンな返事をする。\n→ My grandfather, being hard of hearing, often makes an irrelevant answer.",
 "とんてんかん": "قَعْقَعَ (To make a clanking sound)  [clanking]",
 "とんで": "صِفْر, ٠ (The cardinal number occurring before one and that denotes no quantity or amount ) / صِفْر, ٠ (The numeric symbol that represents the cardinal number zero.)  [zero]\nwhen reading a number aloud; e.g. 20036 = 二万飛んで飛んで三十六 / ذُبَابَة, دبان (Especially, any of the insects of the family Muscidae, such as the common housef) / طَارَ (to travel through air) / طار (to travel through air)  [flying]\nusual meaning; -te form of 飛ぶ",
