 "とんでもありません": "عَفْوًا, عَلَى الرُحْب وَالسَّعَة (A conventional reply to an expression of gratitude.)  [not at all]\nsometimes considered incorrect; とんでもない（こと）です is preferable",
 "とんでもございません": "عَفْوًا, عَلَى الرُحْب وَالسَّعَة (A conventional reply to an expression of gratitude.)  [not at all]\nsometimes considered incorrect; とんでもない（こと）です or とんでもないことでございます is preferable",
 "とんでもない": "لَا يَخْطُرُ عَلَى الْبَالِ (That cannot be believed.) / لَا يَخْطُرُ عَلَى الْبَالِ (Inconceivable or unimaginable; extremely improbable in a way that goes against c)  [unthinkable]\nمثال: ジャックが音楽が苦手なんてとんでもない、それどころか、ピアノを弾くのがうまい。\n→ It isn't true that Jack is no good at music; on the contrary, he plays the piano well. / [absolutely not! ; far from it!]\nمثال: 「君はそれを終えたか」「とんでもない、始めたばかりだ」\n→ \"Have you finished it?\" \"On the contrary, I've just begun.\" / عَفْوًا, عَلَى الرُحْب وَالسَّعَة (A conventional reply to an expression of gratitude.)  [not at all]",
 "とんでもはっぷん": "عَبَثِيّ, سَخِيف (Contrary to reason or propriety; obviously and flatly opposed to manifest truth;)  [absurd]\nハップン is from \"happen\"",
