 "どうぞ": "أَرْضَى, أَعْجَبَ (To make happy or satisfy; to give pleasure to.) / مِن فَضْلِك (interjection to make a polite request) / رَجَاءً (interjection to make a polite request) / لَو سَمَحْت (interjection to make a polite request) / لُطْفًا (interjection to make a polite request) / أَرْجُوك (interjection to make a polite request)  [please]\nمثال: 写真をどうぞ見せて下さい。\n→ Please show me your picture. / بِالتَّأْكِيد (In a way which is certain; with certainty.) / بِالتَّأْكِيد, بِدُون شَكّ (Without doubt, surely.) / بِالتَّأْكِيد, بِدُون شَكّ (An emphatic affirmative answer; of course.)  [certainly]\nwhen giving permission or accepting a request\nمثال: 「電話を使わせてもらってもいいですか」「ええ、どうぞ」\n→ \"Do you mind if I use your phone?\" \"No, please go ahead.\" / تَفَضَّل, تَفَضَّلِي (Said when handing something over to someone or doing a favour to them, usually t)  [here you are]\nwhen handing something to someone\nمثال: 「塩を取って下さい」「はい、どうぞ」\n→ \"Pass me the salt, please.\" \"Here you are.\" / أَعْطَى, وَهَبَ (To move, shift, provide something abstract or concrete to someone or something o)  [to give]",
